---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SectionDivider from "../components/SectionDivider.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Divine Health Homeopathy"
  description="Learn how Divine Health Homeopathy collects, uses, protects, and handles personal information, including information related to consultations and voluntary research participation."
>
  <main>
    <!-- Privacy Policy Hero -->
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-hero-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your Privacy Matters</p>

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <SectionDivider />

        <p class="legal-intro">
          Divine Health Homeopathy, LLC respects your privacy and is committed
          to handling personal information thoughtfully, responsibly, and only
          for appropriate purposes related to communication, education,
          consultations, and other services you choose to use.
        </p>

        <p class="updated">
          Last updated: August 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Privacy Policy Content -->
    <section class="legal-section">
      <div class="legal-container">

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Scope of This Privacy Policy</h2>

          <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how Divine Health Homeopathy, LLC
            ("Divine Health Homeopathy," "we," "our," or "us") may collect,
            use, protect, and disclose personal information when you visit
            <strong> DivineHealthHomeopathy.com</strong>, contact Mindy Wallent,
            or interact with services associated with Divine Health
            Homeopathy.
          </p>

          <p>
            This policy applies to information handled directly by Divine
            Health Homeopathy. Third-party websites, organizations, scheduling
            systems, research organizations, and other services linked from
            this website may maintain their own privacy policies and practices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Information You Choose to Provide</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy may receive personal information when you
            voluntarily contact Mindy by email, telephone, or through another
            communication method.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on the reason for your communication, information you
            provide may include your name, email address, telephone number,
            scheduling information, questions, and information you voluntarily
            share concerning your health or the health concerns for which you
            are seeking homeopathic support.
          </p>

          <p>
            Please use discretion when sending sensitive health or personal
            information through ordinary email. Standard email is not always a
            secure method for transmitting sensitive information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Consultation and Client Information</h2>

          <p>
            If you become a client, additional information may be collected as
            part of the homeopathic consultation and follow-up process. This may
            include health history, symptoms, medications, personal and family
            history, lifestyle information, observations, consultation notes,
            and other information relevant to understanding your individual
            homeopathic case.
          </p>

          <p>
            Information collected during a consultation is used for purposes
            related to providing and managing individualized homeopathic care,
            communicating with you, documenting the case, arranging follow-up,
            and meeting applicable educational, supervisory, professional, or
            research responsibilities.
          </p>

          <p>
            While Mindy is completing her supervised clinical training,
            consultation information may also be reviewed with appropriate
            supervisors or through systems associated with Homeopathy Help
            Network and her educational program as necessary for supervised
            clinical care.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>How Personal Information May Be Used</h2>

          <p>
            Personal information may be used to:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Respond to questions or consultation inquiries.</li>
            <li>Communicate about scheduling and availability.</li>
            <li>Provide and follow up on individualized homeopathic consultations.</li>
            <li>Maintain appropriate consultation and case records.</li>
            <li>Support supervised clinical education when applicable.</li>
            <li>Respond to requests regarding your information.</li>
            <li>Maintain the security and proper operation of the website.</li>
            <li>Comply with applicable legal, ethical, contractual, or research obligations.</li>
            <li>
              Use anonymized clinical information for approved research only
              when appropriate consent has been obtained.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy does not sell personal or health
            information to advertisers or data brokers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Website and Technical Information</h2>

          <p>
            When you visit this website, the technology used to host and
            deliver the site may process ordinary technical information
            associated with a web request. This can include information such as
            an Internet Protocol (IP) address, browser or device type, requested
            page, date and time of access, and related diagnostic or security
            information.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Divine Health Homeopathy website is hosted using Microsoft
            Azure. Technical information may therefore be processed by hosting
            and infrastructure providers as necessary to deliver, secure, and
            maintain the website.
          </p>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy does not currently use the website to
            create visitor accounts or directly process online payments.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy does not currently use advertising cookies
            or behavioral advertising systems on this website.
          </p>

          <p>
            Basic technical functionality provided by browsers, hosting
            infrastructure, or third-party services may use cookies or similar
            technologies when necessary for their operation. If Divine Health
            Homeopathy later adds analytics, advertising, or other tracking
            technologies that materially change how visitor information is
            collected or used, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Required HOHM Research Disclosure -->
        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Use of Anonymized Clinical Information for Research</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy supports responsible research that
            contributes to a better understanding of homeopathic clinical
            practice. Participation in research involving your clinical
            information is voluntary and requires appropriate consent.
          </p>

          <div class="research-disclosure">
            <p class="disclosure-label">
  <a
    href="https://advancehomeopathy.org/disclosures/"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    HOHM Foundation Office of Research Disclosure
  </a>
</p>

            <p>
              “I am a clinician that also engages in research. I work alongside
              HOHM Foundation Office of Research. All research conducted by
              HOHM Foundation Office of Research involving human subjects is
              undertaken according to human research protocols and is formally
              approved by the Canadian College of Naturopathic Medicine’s
              Research Ethics Board. Clients/patients may consent to have the
              anonymized clinical information from their case used for research
              purposes. I protect clients’/patients’ rights to privacy by
              withholding names and all other identifying information.
              Clients/patients have the right to give or withdraw consent to
              have case information used for research purposes at any time. By
              consenting, clients/patients do not waive any rights to legal
              recourse in the event of research-related harm (TCPS2-2022,
              article 3.2 (k)). If you have any inquiries about this research
              or would like to withdraw your consent, please contact HOHM
              Foundation Office of Research at
              research@hohmfoundation.org.”
            </p>
            <p class="disclosure-source">
  View the official HOHM Foundation research disclosures and PGRN statement
  <a
    href="https://advancehomeopathy.org/disclosures/"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    here
  </a>.
</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            Consent to the use of anonymized clinical information for research
            is separate from consenting to receive homeopathic care. A client
            may decline or later withdraw research consent as described above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy does not disclose personal information
            except when reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this
            policy, when you have authorized the disclosure, or when disclosure
            is required or permitted by law.
          </p>

          <p>
            Information may be shared with appropriate service providers,
            supervisors, educational or clinical systems, or research partners
            when necessary to support the services you have requested and when
            appropriate privacy protections apply.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples may include website hosting providers, email services,
            Homeopathy Help Network, clinical supervisors, and the HOHM
            Foundation Office of Research when research participation has been
            appropriately authorized.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Homeopathy Help Network and Other Third Parties</h2>

          <p>
            The Divine Health Homeopathy website contains links to Homeopathy
            Help Network and other outside organizations and educational
            resources.
          </p>

          <p>
            When you leave DivineHealthHomeopathy.com and interact with another
            website or service, information you provide to that organization is
            governed by its own privacy practices and policies. Divine Health
            Homeopathy does not control the privacy practices of independent
            third-party websites.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Information Concerning Children</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy provides homeopathic consultations for
            families and may work with children when a parent or legal guardian
            participates in the consultation.
          </p>

          <p>
            This website is intended for adults and is not designed for
            children to independently submit personal information. Parents and
            legal guardians should provide information concerning minors when
            communicating with Divine Health Homeopathy about a child's care.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Data Security</h2>

          <p>
            Reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures
            are used to protect personal information from unauthorized access,
            loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.
          </p>

          <p>
            No method of transmitting or storing information electronically can
            be guaranteed to be completely secure. For that reason, sensitive
            personal or health information should be shared only through
            communication methods appropriate for the information being
            transmitted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Retention of Information</h2>

          <p>
            Personal information is retained only for as long as reasonably
            necessary for the purposes for which it was collected and for any
            applicable educational, professional, research, legal, recordkeeping,
            or administrative requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            Information that is no longer required may be securely deleted,
            destroyed, or anonymized when appropriate.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Access, Correction, and Privacy Requests</h2>

          <p>
            You may contact Divine Health Homeopathy if you have questions about
            personal information maintained about you or if you wish to request
            access to or correction of information, subject to any applicable
            legal, professional, research, or recordkeeping requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you previously consented to the use of anonymized clinical
            information for HOHM Foundation research and wish to withdraw that
            consent, please follow the research contact instructions provided
            in the research disclosure above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block">
          <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

          <p>
            Divine Health Homeopathy may revise this Privacy Policy from time
            to time to reflect changes in website functionality, services,
            technology, research activities, or privacy practices.
          </p>

          <p>
            When meaningful changes are made, the date shown at the top of this
            page will be updated.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-block legal-contact">
          <h2>Privacy Questions</h2>

          <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how Divine Health
            Homeopathy handles personal information, please contact:
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Divine Health Homeopathy, LLC</strong><br />
            Attn: Mindy Wallent<br />
            <a href="mailto:Mindy@DivineHealthHomeopathy.com">
              Mindy@DivineHealthHomeopathy.com
            </a><br />
            <a href="tel:+17347676085">(734) 767-6085</a>
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .legal-hero {
    padding: 86px 40px 82px;

    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at top,
        #fffdf8 0%,
        #f6eee1 58%,
        #eadbc6 100%
      );

    text-align: center;
  }

  .legal-hero-inner {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 16px;

    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.34em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1,
  h2 {
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 26px;

    font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6vw, 5.1rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .legal-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 30px auto 0;

    color: #40516a;
    font-size: 1.17rem;
    line-height: 1.84;
  }

  .updated {
    margin: 24px 0 0;

    color: #756b5c;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .legal-section {
    padding: 92px 40px 112px;

    background: #fffdf9;
  }

  .legal-container {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-block {
    padding: 0 0 46px;
    margin: 0 0 46px;

    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184, 154, 94, 0.24);
  }

  .legal-block:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;

    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-block h2 {
    margin: 0 0 20px;

    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.35rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .legal-block p,
  .legal-block li {
    color: #4a596f;
    font-size: 1.04rem;
    line-height: 1.82;
  }

  .legal-block p {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }

  .legal-block p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .legal-block ul {
    margin: 8px 0 22px;
    padding-left: 26px;
  }

  .legal-block li {
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    padding-left: 5px;
  }

  .legal-block a {
    color: var(--navy);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(184, 154, 94, 0.65);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal-block a:hover {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .research-disclosure {
    margin: 28px 0;

    padding: 30px 32px;

    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at top left,
        #fffaf3 0%,
        #f4e8d5 100%
      );

    border: 1px solid #dfd0b7;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: 0 22px 22px 0;

    box-shadow:
      0 14px 34px rgba(16, 35, 63, 0.06);
  }

  .research-disclosure .disclosure-label {
    margin-bottom: 14px;

    color: var(--navy);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .research-disclosure p:last-child {
    color: #46566d;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.78;
  }

  .legal-contact {
    padding: 34px;

    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at top,
        #fffaf3 0%,
        #f5ead9 100%
      );

    border: 1px solid #dfd0b7;
    border-radius: 24px;

    box-shadow:
      0 16px 42px rgba(16, 35, 63, 0.07);
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .legal-hero {
      padding: 62px 20px 64px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 3.15rem;
    }

    .legal-intro {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .legal-section {
      padding: 68px 20px 82px;
    }

    .legal-block {
      padding-bottom: 36px;
      margin-bottom: 36px;
    }

    .legal-block p,
    .legal-block li {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .research-disclosure {
      padding: 24px 22px;
    }

    .legal-contact {
      padding: 26px 22px;
    }
  }
</style>